---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const email = 'rdm355190@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What Write-Ahead is, and who's writing it.">
  <a class="back-link" href="/">← the log</a>
  <h1 style="margin-top:14px;">About</h1>

  <section class="author-card" data-sketch-frame>
    <div class="avatar-ring" data-sketch-frame="circle" data-sketch-stroke="--accent">
      <div class="avatar-wrap">
        <img src="/avatar.webp" alt="Danish Mehmood" width="160" height="160" loading="eager" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="author-text">
      <h2 class="author-name">Write-Ahead</h2>
      <p class="author-role">database internals · one entry at a time</p>
      <p>
        I kept using databases without really knowing what happened after I pressed
        <code>Enter</code> on a query. So I started taking the engine apart — the page
        format, the B-tree, the write-ahead log, the lock manager — and drawing each piece
        until it made sense.
      </p>
      <p>
        Write-Ahead is that teardown, written in public. The bet is simple: if I can
        <em>draw</em> how a part works, I actually understand it — and so will you.
      </p>
      <p class="contact">
        Say hi · <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    <b>Write-Ahead</b> is a hand-drawn tour of how a database works on the inside.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every entry takes one mechanism the docs gloss over and rebuilds it from first
    principles — with sketches, byte layouts, and small animations you can poke at. Less
    "here's the API," more "here's what the bytes are doing on disk." The goal is that you
    leave able to <em>picture</em> the engine, not just call it.
  </p>

  <style>
    .author-card {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      gap: 26px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      background: var(--panel);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 24px 24px 20px;
      margin: 1.6em 0 2.4em;
      box-shadow: 0 12px 30px -22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    }
    .avatar-ring {
      position: relative;
      flex: none;
      padding: 11px;            /* room for the sketched ring to sit outside the photo */
      border-radius: 50%;
    }
    .avatar-wrap {
      position: relative;
      width: 160px;
      height: 160px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .avatar-wrap img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
    }
    /* warm, blog-themed overlay so the photo blends into the palette */
    .avatar-wrap::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background:
        radial-gradient(120% 120% at 30% 15%, transparent 38%,
          color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, transparent) 100%),
        linear-gradient(160deg,
          color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent),
          color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent2) 18%, transparent));
      mix-blend-mode: overlay;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .author-text { flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 0; }
    .author-name {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 2.6rem);
      margin: 0 0 2px;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    .author-role {
      font-family: var(--font-hand);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .author-text p { margin: 0 0 0.9em; }
    .contact {
      font-family: var(--font-hand);
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }
    .contact a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; word-break: break-all; }

    @media (max-width: 460px) {
      .author-card { justify-content: center; text-align: center; }
      .author-text { text-align: left; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
